<%= l_ui_title_bar(
  title: "Cards",
  breadcrumbs: [
    ["Home", root_path]
  ]
) %>

<p class="mt-4">
  A content card in two styles that share one colour system. The base <code>l-ui-card</code> is
  bordered; add <code>l-ui-card--gradient</code> to paint a soft tint fill behind the same border.
  Colour comes from a separate, reusable <strong>tint</strong> slot, so the style and colour axes
  compose independently. Toggle the theme to see both adapt.
</p>

<p class="mt-2">
  The tint slots (<code>l-ui-tint-1</code> to <code>l-ui-tint-5</code>) are a decorative palette
  shared across components, <strong>independent of the brand <code>--accent</code></strong> (which
  drives interactive things like primary buttons and active tabs). The slot numbers are
  <strong>palette positions, not fixed hues</strong> - the gem ships sensible defaults (teal, green,
  amber, rose, purple) and you re-skin any slot once in your overrides file without the class name
  ever going stale. A card with no tint slot falls back to the neutral border and foreground colours.
</p>

<h2 class="mt-8 l-ui-heading--section">Bordered cards</h2>

<p class="mt-2">
  The default style: a tint-coloured border and title over the plain surface. Pair the title with
  an optional <code>l-ui-card__icon</code> (painted in the tint colour) and a
  <code>l-ui-card__body</code>.
</p>

